TITLE='Authentic title "Stop Thinking Poor: The Mindset of the 1%" is an imperative plus an elite-identity frame ("the 1%"). The script delivers 11 "mental shifts" contrasting "poor" and "wealthy" thinking; it never defines the 1% or gives a wealth or income threshold. TYPICAL against the cohort. Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a white shirt and jeans, relaxed and smug, lying in a green hammock. Right: a heavy black headline "THINK RICH" and a curved arrow pointing at an open green safe spilling gold coins; a small green piggy bank sits bottom left. At 320x180 the two-word headline, hammock and safe stay legible. "THINK RICH" restates the title\'s mindset promise; the passive-income hammock image matches the "money works while you sleep" theme.'
SCRIPT='A list essay of 11 mindset "shifts": hook (others glide through life); assets vs liabilities; decades-long time horizon (tax refund as loan); financial education and 80/20 behaviour; creating vs consuming; risk (savings 0.5% vs 3% inflation; 10% market average); taxes ($200K at 40% vs $150K at 20%); leverage; generosity and abundance; information and action; money velocity ($5,000 example); strategic impatience; challenge close. Few numbers. Directly verified: CPI inflation ~3% at upload (FRED). Wrong: the tax example leaves both earners with exactly $120,000, so "keeping less" is false. Unsupported: "80% behaviour". Moralising "poor people" framing; much repetition. The stored ending is complete.'
